    "title": "Date announced for Alabama Crimson Tide 'takeover' of SEC Network - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Steve Holley ,\n19 hours ago Nov 29, 2025; Auburn, Alabama, USA; Alabama defensive back Bray Hubbard (18) returns a pass her intercepted at Jordan-Hare Stadium. Alabama defeated Auburn 27-20. Mandatory Credit: Gary Cosby Jr.-Tuscaloosa News By Gary Cosby Jr.-Tuscaloosa News, Gary Cosby Jr.-Tuscaloosa News / USA TODAY NETWORK via Imagn Images The Alabama Crimson Tide are about to take over SEC Network.\nThe 12th annual \"SEC Network Takeover\" days begin this week, and 24 hours of Crimson Tide athletic events from the past year will be featured on the ESPN-owned channel. The date for Alabama 's takeover is Friday, July 3.\nThe event will begin at 12 a.m. ET/11 p.m. CT with a rebroadcast of Alabama football 's 24-21 win over the Georgia Bulldogs at Sanford Stadium from Sept. 27.\nThe Tide's win in Athens is the first of three football games from the 2025 season that will be rebroadcast. Alabama's 27-20 Iron Bowl win over Auburn at Jordan-Hare Stadium will be shown beginning at 4 a.m. CT, and its 34-24 come-from-behind win over Oklahoma in the College Football Playoff will cap the 24-hour marathon beginning at 8 p.m.\nTwo Alabama men's basketball games will be featured from the 2025-26 season, including the Crimson Tide's thrilling double-overtime win over the Arkansas Razorbacks at Coleman Coliseum from Feb. 18.\nSee the full schedule of Alabama games and events.\n'SEC Network Takeover' schedule: dates for all 16 teams July 3: Alabama July 4: Arkansas July 5: Auburn July 6: Florida July 7: Georgia July 8: Kentucky July 9: LSU July 10: Ole Miss July 11: Mississippi State July 12: Missouri July 13: Oklahoma July 14: South Carolina July 15: Tennessee July 16: Texas July 17: Texas A&M July 18: Vanderbilt Follow us at @ RollTideWire on X, and like our page on Facebook , for ongoing coverage of Alabama Crimson Tide news, notes and opinions.\nThis article originally appeared on Roll Tide Wire: Date announced for Alabama Crimson Tide 'takeover' of SEC Network\n1",
    "summary": "19 hours ago Nov 29, 2025; Auburn, Alabama, USA; Alabama defensive back Bray Hubbard (18) returns a pass her intercepted at Jordan-Hare Stadium. The 12th annual \"SEC Network Takeover\" days begin this week, and 24 hours of Crimson Tide athletic events from the past year will be featured on the ESPN-owned channel. The event will begin at 12 a.m. ET/11 p.m. CT with a rebroadcast of Alabama football 's 24-21 win over the Georgia Bulldogs at Sanford Stadium from Sept. 27.",
